# Ubuntu packages baked into the appbox image, one package name per line.
#
# Only packages from Ubuntu's own archive go here (whatever
# `apt-cache policy <name>` finds inside the box). Check a name first:
#     distrobox enter apps -- apt-cache policy vlc
# A "Candidate:" line with a version means it is in the archive.
#
# Format:
#   - one package name per line, nothing else on the line;
#   - lines starting with # and blank lines are ignored;
#   - no comments after a name: `vlc  # video player` would hand "#",
#     "video" and "player" to apt-get as package names and fail the build.
#
# Examples (remove the leading "# " to install one):
# vlc
# gimp
# htop
#
# A GUI app also needs its launcher exported: add its .desktop file to
# exported_apps in distrobox.ini, in a separate pull request that merges
# only after the image with the package has built green. Find the file with
#     distrobox enter apps -- dpkg -L vlc | grep '\.desktop$'
# See "Adding an app" in README.md.
#
# Not in this file: apps from other places, like the two already in the box.
#   - Signal Desktop comes from Signal's own apt repo. Its key, repo and
#     `apt-get install signal-desktop` are in scripts/appbox.sh. Copy that
#     block for another vendor repo whose license allows a public image.
#   - Claude Desktop is proprietary, so it is never baked into the public
#     image. scripts/appbox.sh only adds Anthropic's key and repo, and the
#     box installs the app on first start with the init hook
#     scripts/claude-desktop-sync (see init_hooks in distrobox.ini).
